WEBVTT

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.570
Huh? We're out of rice.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.860
What? We haven't gotten
any new supplies in yet?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.040
Sakamoto-san! We're out of rice!

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.040
Huh?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.170
I didn't think everyone
would be gathering today...

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.630
This is bad.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.630
What should we do?

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.590
We need a few things. Can you girls go shopping for us?

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.880
Shopping?

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.010
Roger!

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.480
So, we need you to head out and procure some local supplies.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.320
Shirley-san is trained to operate large trucks.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.370
Lucchini-san, you're the
resident Romagna expert,

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.490
so I'd like you two to
undertake this mission.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.700
Roger!

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.250
All right! I haven't driven in ages!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.290
Sorry, we'd send more people,

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.420
but we don't know when the enemy's going to attack.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.880
Yay! Driving, driving!

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.470
It's nice to go off base
from time to time.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.220
I'm delighted to take this mission!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.060
Lastly, I'd like Miyafuji-san and Lynne-san to join you.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.480
Excuse me. I'd rather wait here, on standby.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.810
Huh? Why?

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:49.480
Huh?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.900
Understood. So just you, Miyafuji-san.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.980
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.230
Guide them around town, Lucchini.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:59.030
You can count on me!

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.080
Miyafuji, you are to follow
Shirley's orders out there.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:04.740
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.200
Now, please get your orders in.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.870
Orders, huh? Some new
training tools would be nice...

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.460
Yes, but not like that. Things to use while we recharge.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.460
Recharge?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.470
The best way to recharge is to train hard and rest hard.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.430
Well, actual baths for people, to keep
morale high after training, would be nice.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.100
Is training all you guys think about?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.190
Please think of more practical items.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:34.980
Excuse me...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.070
I would like some black tea.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.990
Good call. We could
all use some tea-time.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.450
For me, I'd like a radio.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.950
Don't you have a fancy Karlsland one?

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.950
I mean a radio we can leave out here.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.790
Wouldn't you guys like to be able to hear music and the news?

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.540
Oh, that's what you mean.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.290
That would be nice.
Please see to it, Miyafuji.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.340
Yes, ma'am. Black tea
and a radio, right?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.430
A piano. Please get me a piano.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.550
They're not going to
be able to lug a piano.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.270
Boo, I wanted to hear Sanya play...

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.020
Say, Sanya, anything you want?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.310
Eila, why don't you ask
for something <i>you</i> want?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.270
What about you, Barkhorn-san?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.820
Me? Nothing really comes to mind...

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.070
What about a gift for Chris-san?

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.820
Ch-Chris-san, huh? Right...

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.490
H-How about something
cute for her to wear...

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:31.160
Huh?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.210
An outfit, please!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.630
An outfit... What sort of outfit?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.790
I'll let you decide.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.920
She's about your size,
so I'll let you decide.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.920
Are you sure?

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.050
Y-Yes. I'll trust your opinion.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.810
Understood.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.180
Oh, what about you, Perrine-san?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.310
I don't need anything.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.020
Huh? But we're going into town, so...

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.110
I said I don't need anything!

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.740
Perrine-san...

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:12.620
She donated all her savings and paychecks to the reconstruction efforts in Gallia.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.660
I had no idea.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.750
Oh, I know, Yoshika-chan.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.540
Please get me some flower seeds, in addition to the black tea.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.000
Sure.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.800
So, umm, I still need
Hartmann-san's request.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.840
Is Hartmann still in bed?

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.260
Wake up, Hartmann!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.270
Eh... Just give me
another ninety minutes...

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.440
A soldier should be swift on her feet!

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.270
Get up at once!

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:42.190
Umm, I am going on a shopping trip. Is there anything you want?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.780
Sweet stuff!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.700
What you need is an alarm clock!

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:50.780
But I want sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets!

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.700
Shut up!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.200
But I want sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! Sweets!

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.830
Yeah, get her an alarm clock.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.210
R-Right...

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.540
Alarm... clock...

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:02.500
Miyafuji!

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.000
Huh?!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:03.750
A pillow.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.880
Huh?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.010
Buy me a pillow. A pillow.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.010
A pillow?

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.100
Ideally a black one, with a red section.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.060
Made of velvet, if they have it. Otherwise, anything soft.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.690
And stuffed with water fowl feathers, like down or any small feathers.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.940
H-Hold on!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.020
Did you get all that?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.280
Eila-san, that's a lot of details to take in at once...

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.240
Fine...

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.200
I'll write it out for you,
so don't screw it up.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.370
All right? Don't forget, now. Promise!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:38.750
Yeah...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.630
See you guys later.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.380
We'll be back in a bit!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.380
Come back safe.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.400
It's so beautiful!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.860
I can't believe Lynne-chan's missing this!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.070
Clear visibility ahead,
with no oncoming traffic...

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:17.950
What was that?

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.710
Here we go!

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.550
W-We're gonna fall off the cliff!

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.050
This is awesome!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.390
Huh?!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.760
Go!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.680
Stop!
Go!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.680
Stop!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.650
<i>Go!</i>

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.860
Yay!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.150
Landed it.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.080
Ugh... I don't feel so good...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.790
Yoshika! Yoshika! We're in Rome.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.000
Huh?

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.920
Wow! Wow, it's so beautiful!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.890
Oh? Is this your first
time in Rome, Yoshika?

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.720
Yeah. Hey, what's that?

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.930
That's an ancient battle arena.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.430
Huh? What about that?

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.600
That's a civic meeting hall.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.480
This is all so cool!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.150
You sound like a kid, Yoshika.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.070
Rome is an historical city, after all.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.240
Isn't it? Isn't it?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.740
It's such an incredible city.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.870
Lucchini-chan, you were born here, right?

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.370
Guilty as charged.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:44.370
She bragged about Rome 24/7, while we were in Africa.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.420
Can you blame me?
Rome is just that special!

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.960
Right, right. Understood.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.880
Is this place okay?

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.930
Yup. They'll have most of what we need.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.600
Wow! This is so cool!

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.480
Let's see...

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:05.980
This looks like a radio.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.860
These are for me!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.070
Make sure to get some for Hartmann, too.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.860
Lucchini, hold this for me.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.190
With pleasure!

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:16.280
Tea, flowers, and clothing...

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:20.530
Hey, that'll look good on you, Miyafuji.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.250
Oh, no. Barkhorn-san asked me to buy this.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.460
What? What?!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.040
This? On her?!

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.010
Huh?

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:37.430
Not her! This is for her little sister, Chris-san, to wear.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.260
I-I can't breathe...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.470
It's not for her!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.770
Th-That's hilarious!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.640
Hilarious!

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.150
Unhand me!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:59.700
Super... Lucchini... Kick!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.030
One more!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.160
Got 'em.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.790
E-Excuse me...

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.500
Come with me?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:06.960
Huh?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.460
Right this way!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.710
Huh?!

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.210
W-Wait...

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.600
Th-Thank you for your help.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.310
Umm, who are you?

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.400
Me?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.690
A good Samaritan who
happened to be passing by...

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.240
Francesca Lucchini!

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.660
My name is Maria.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.530
Maria, huh? Nice to meet you!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.990
U-Umm, it's a pleasure
to get to know you.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.000
Hey, what was that whole
mess about before?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.000
U-Umm...

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.840
Wait, I know! Those two are in the mafia!

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.130
Am I right? Am I right?

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.920
U-Umm, it would seem so.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.630
I knew it!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.510
Those back alleys can
be really dangerous.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.050
You have to be careful!

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.430
You're right. Thank you.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.650
Say, since you're shopping,
why don't we shop together?

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.030
Oh, no, I'm not shopping.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.280
Hmm? So what are you doing, then?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.660
Umm... I guess you could say
sightseeing... Or just going for a walk...

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.700
Going for a walk?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.540
Huh? Yes.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.500
I haven't been out of my house much, so I don't know Rome very well.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.170
Huh...

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.300
It's strange to not know the city you were born in, huh?

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.340
Leave it to Lucchini-sama, then!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.260
Come on. Let's go.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.690
Huh? She's not in the truck, either.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.030
She was sitting in the shop before, right?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:07.530
Man, I gave all the money
we had left to her, too.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:11.000
What?! But we haven't
bought food supplies yet!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.670
My gut tells me she'll be back soon, but...

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.210
Let's go look for her!

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:29.010
Huge, isn't it?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.770
It's wonderful.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.190
Lucchini-chan...

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.330
Where did you go?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.330
They say if you turn your
back to it and toss a coin in,

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.210
you'll return to Rome someday.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.080
Really?

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.010
Shirley-san!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:08.800
Did you find her?

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.930
I found a cat!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.110
Here you go.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.110
Wow! Thanks!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:24.570
Grazie.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.850
It's so hot!

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.060
Bye-bye!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.100
Ciao!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.100
Arrivederci.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.480
I'm out of cash.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:11.620
I can't find her anywhere.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.330
I've asked a bunch of
people if they've seen her.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.580
I'm running out of steam.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.460
This is delicious!

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.380
Shirley-san, you have to try this!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.210
You know...

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.300
Here!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.220
Wow! This is incredible.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.310
Isn't it?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.180
Excuse me! Another piece of this cake!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.270
Actually, make it two more.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.100
Please!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.150
What do you think, Maria?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.410
This is my absolute favorite view.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.320
It's gorgeous.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:56.450
I don't want to go home.
I want to stay here forever.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.500
Stay here forever, then.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.460
That's a good point.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:05.960
I wonder if I'll be able to protect Rome and all its beauty.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:06.630
Huh?

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.880
Ah! There's smoke
coming from that house!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.720
That's just because they're cooking.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:17.060
So those are the homes of the <i>body politic</i>.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.430
"Body politic"?

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.480
I had no idea.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:21.940
What the heck is that?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.070
Hey, there's one more
view I want to show you.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.440
I'd love to see it.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.660
But I can't take you there right now...

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.120
Oh, I see.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.540
I look forward to seeing it next time, then.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:37.990
Yeah!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.920
Geez... They're moving into Rome?

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:47.840
Huh?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:48.800
Neuroi!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:49.630
Oh no!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.720
Let's go, Miyafuji.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:52.510
Right!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.430
Let's hurry and get
out of here, Lucchini-san.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.680
I have to go!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.730
I see her! Over there, Shirley-san!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.810
On top of the basilica!

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:03.400
Basilica?

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:10.530
Shirley!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.650
Watch out!

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.110
I have to go. I'm a Witch.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.120
Huh?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.280
Hold this for me.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:18.950
A Witch?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.330
Yup!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:26.380
That's why I have to protect Romagna!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.940
Lucchini-san?

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.440
I will protect Romagna!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.150
Wait for us, Lucchini!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:51.820
But...

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.610
I understand. But you cannot fight alone.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:58.660
We want to protect your
hometown with you, Lucchini-chan!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.160
Thank you, Shirley, Yoshika!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.330
All right. Let's attack it together.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.640
That's it!

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.600
Shirley, I spotted the core.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.680
All right. X-Attack!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.190
Lucchini-chan!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.980
All right... Come on, come on, come on!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.150
I've been spotted.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.720
Amazing...

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:07.060
Yoshika, hold this for me.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.770
Huh? U-Uh...

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:12.980
I wanna show you something.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:13.440
Huh?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.280
U-Umm!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.830
Look, Maria.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.290
This is the view I wanted you to see.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.710
This is...

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.090
You aren't scared, Lucchini-san?

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.970
Huh? Of what?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:41.970
You don't get scared fighting such a terrifying enemy?

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:46.220
If we don't defeat the Neuroi,
Romagna will be gone forever.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:50.850
It's up to us Witches to protect
everyone's friends and families.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.690
So it's like <i>noblesse oblige</i>?

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:55.780
Huh?

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.650
You like those fancy words, huh?

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.990
Do I?

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:05.870
Whoops.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.330
Can you make it home okay alone?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.460
Yes.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.840
I had an amazing time today.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:15.920
Really?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:16.840
Yes.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.970
I realized what I have to do.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.590
Yeah? Good luck.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:24.760
Thank you!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:31.560
Bye-bye, Maria! See you again!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.370
Wah! I'm so sorry!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:54.960
Still, for her to spend all the food money...

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.000
That's your superiors' fault!

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.710
Me included.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:01.300
Let's review what went wrong together.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.800
Sorry, Lucchini.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.220
Here you go, Eila-san.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:10.770
So they had what I asked for?

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:13.940
You found what she wanted? That's great.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.610
This is yours, Sanya-chan.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.320
Thank you, Yoshika-chan.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:21.570
Your request was really specific, Eila-san...

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.240
I-I don't think it was.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:28.280
Eila, you need to be a little more
flexible when asking someone's help.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.040
Perrine-san, this is for you.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.460
What is it?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:35.920
Flower seeds.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:40.510
Lynne-chan thought it might be nice if she plants flowers outside the base.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.760
You did, Lynne-san?

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:47.390
Yeah. I was hoping you'd
show me how to plant them.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:49.810
Why would you bring me into that?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:51.640
Let's plant them together.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.480
Please teach me.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:57.610
I guess I have no choice.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:01.070
For starters, these marigolds need to be planted in direct sunlight.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:05.860
And the chamomile and bergamot need to be in indirect sunlight during summer.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.200
Sweets... Sweets...

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.370
What do you think, Barkhorn-san?

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.710
O-Oh, it looks great.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.170
Won't it be a little tight in the chest?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.800
What are you talking about?! It's perfect.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.170
Oh, yeah... I think you're right.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.090
It's working!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:30.760
Now, Her Highness, Duchess Maria, in her first day of official duty

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:36.020
in the Principality of Romagna, will address the people from the garden party.

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:41.360
Rome was attacked by the Neuroi yesterday.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:48.070
However, one small Witch's actions helped thwart the attack.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:53.830
I learned a valuable lesson from her while this was all transpiring.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:59.380
We each must do everything in our power to protect the world.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:05.880
I will do everything I can, starting today, to defend Romagna.

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:09.800
So, I thank you, my dear friend,

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:12.850
Ensign Francesca Lucchini.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:13.770
Huh?

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.810
What?!

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:16.980
Huh?

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:29.610
As a small token of gratitude,

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:33.540
I send these gifts to the
501st Joint Fighter Wing.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:38.000
S-So heavy...

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.600
Sanya's clinging on to the pillow I bought.

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:19.270
Pressed up against my pillow are Sanya's slender arms... and her chest...!

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:20.060
Her very heart is pressed against it as it...

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Next time on <i>Strike Witches 2:</i>
Higher than the Sky.
